WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.040
( theme music playing )

2
00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.240
( both yelling )

3
00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.280
( applause. cheering )

4
00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.640
Well struck.

5
00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.240
Well struck. Dog.

6
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.920
Did you like that?

7
00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.920
It was well struck. your Grace.

8
00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.080
I already said it was well struck.

9
00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.080
Yes. your Grace.

10
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.680
-Who's next?
-Herald: Lothor Brune.

11
00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.880
Freerider in the service
Of Lord Baelish.

12
00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.040
Ser Dontos the Red of house Hollard.

13
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.680
Ser Dontos the Red of house Hollard!

14
00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.720
Dontos:
Here I am. Here I am.

15
00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.320
Sorry. your Grace.

16
00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.240
My deepest apologies.

17
00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.360
-Joffrey: Are you drunk?
-No.

18
00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.480
Uh. no. No. your Grace.

19
00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.960
-I had two cups of wine.
-Two cups?

20
00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.440
That's not much at all.

21
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.480
Please. have another cup.

22
00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.960
Are you sure. your Grace?

23
00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.240
Joffrey:
Yes. To celebrate my name day.

24
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.720
Have two. Have as much as you like.

25
00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.960
I would be honored. your Grace.

26
00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.720
Ser Meryn. help Ser Dontos
celebrate my name day.

27
00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.840
See that he drinks his fill.

28
00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.480
( crowd gasps )

29
00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.880
( gurgling )

30
00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.920
You can't.

31
00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.400
What did you say?

32
00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:50.480
Did you say I can't?

33
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.080
I only meant it would be bad luck

34
00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.880
To kill a man on your name day.

35
00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.000
What kind of stupid
Peasant's superstition...

36
00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.880
Hound:
The girl is right.

37
00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.480
What a man sows on his name day

38
00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.400
He reaps all year.

39
00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.800
-( men laughing )
-( wine pouring )

40
00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.120
-( Dontos gagging )
-Take him away.

41
00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.760
I'll have him killed
Tomorrow. the fool.

42
00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.800
( crowd murmuring )

43
00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:16.120
He is. A fool--
You're so clever to see it.

44
00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.400
He'll make a much better fool
Than a knight.

45
00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.440
He doesn't deserve
The mercy of a quick death.

46
00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.720
Did you hear my lady. Ser Dontos?

47
00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.680
From this day.
You'll be my new fool.

48
00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.280
Thank you. your Grace.

49
00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.000
And you. my lady. thank you.

50
00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.680
Tyrion:
Beloved nephew.

51
00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.600
We looked for you
On the battlefield.

52
00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.120
And you were nowhere to be found.

53
00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.160
I've... Been here.
Ruling the kingdoms.

54
00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.880
What a fine job you've done.

55
00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.360
Look at you.

56
00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.480
More beautiful than ever.

57
00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:05.320
And you! You-- you're going to be
Bigger than the hound.

58
00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.280
-but much better looking.
-( laughs )

59
00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.480
-This one doesn't like me.
-Can't imagine why.

60
00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.920
-We heard you were dead.
-I'm glad you're not dead.

61
00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.480
Me. too. dear. Death is so boring.

62
00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:21.000
especially now
with so much excitement in the world.

63
00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.720
My lady. I'm sorry for your loss.

64
00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.120
Her loss?

65
00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.440
-Her father was a confessed traitor.
-But still her father.

66
00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.320
Surely having so recently
Lost your own beloved father

67
00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.160
You can sympathize.

68
00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.120
My father was a traitor.

69
00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.880
My mother and brother
are traitors. too.

70
00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.240
I am loyal to my beloved Joffrey.

71
00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.200
Of course you are.

72
00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.880
Well. enjoy your name day.
Your Grace.

73
00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.560
Wish I could stay and celebrate.

74
00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.360
But there is work to be done.

75
00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.360
What work?

76
00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:01.360
Why are you here?

77
00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.120
Pycelle:
The raven arrived from the Citadel

78
00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.000
-This morning. your Grace.
-( bird squawking )

79
00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.000
The conclave has met.
Considered reports

80
00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.840
From maesters all over
The seven kingdoms.

81
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.280
And declared this great summer

82
00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.040
Done... At last.

83
00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:24.000
The longest summer in living memory.

84
00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.000
The peasants say. a long summer means

85
00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.520
-An even longer winter.
-Pycelle: A common superstition.

86
00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:31.400
Littlefinger:
We'll have enough wheat
For a five-year winter.

87
00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.200
If it lasts any longer.

88
00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.200
We'll have fewer peasants.

89
00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:39.520
The city's drowning in refugees.
Your Grace. fleeing the war.

90
00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:42.520
We have nowhere to house them.
And with winter coming.
It'll only get worse.

91
00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.400
You command the city watch.
Do you not. Lord Slynt?

92
00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.720
I do. your Grace.

93
00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.680
And are you not
A lord at my command?

94
00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.960
I owe my title and lands
To your generosity. your Grace.

95
00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.400
Then do your job.
Shut the gates to the peasants.

96
00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.600
They belong in the field.
Not our capital.

97
00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.560
-Yes. your Grace.
-( man whistling tune )

98
00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.400
Don't get up.

99
00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:13.280
More ravishing than ever.
Big sister.

100
00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.320
War agrees with you.

101
00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.840
Forgive the interruption. Carry on.

102
00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:26.800
-What are you doing here?
-Ah. it's been a remarkable journey.

103
00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.400
I pissed off the edge of the wall.

104
00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.480
I slept in a sky cell.

105
00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.880
I fought with the hill tribes--

106
00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.520
So many adventures.

107
00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.920
So much to be thankful for.

108
00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.720
What are you doing here?
This is the small council.

109
00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.240
Yes. well. I do believe
The hand of the king

110
00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.280
Is welcome at all
Small council meetings.

111
00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.080
Our father is hand of the king.

112
00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:53.200
Yes. but in his absence...

113
00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:02.120
Varys:
Your father has named Lord Tyrion

114
00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:04.800
To serve as hand
In his stead while he fights.

115
00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.240
Out! All of you out!

116
00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:14.800
Cersei: I would like to know
How you tricked father into this.

117
00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.440
Tyrion:
If I were capable of tricking father.

118
00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.520
I'd be emperor of the world by now.

119
00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:20.960
You brought this on yourself.

120
00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.800
-I've done nothing.
-Quite right-- you did nothing

121
00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.960
When your son called
For Ned Stark's head.

122
00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.920
Now the entire north
Has risen up against us.

123
00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.320
-I tried to stop it.
-Did you? You failed.

124
00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.440
That bit of theater will haunt
Our family for a generation.

125
00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:37.840
-Robb Stark is a child.
-Who's won every battle he's fought.

126
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.000
Do you understand
We're losing the war?

127
00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:42.760
-What do you know about warfare?
-Nothing.

128
00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:44.440
But I know people.

129
00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.280
And I know that
Our enemies hate each other

130
00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.960
Almost as much as they hate us.

131
00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.600
-Joffrey is king.
-Joffrey is king.

132
00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.200
You are here to advise him.

133
00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:00.400
I'm only here to advise him.

134
00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.360
And if the king listens
To what I say.

135
00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.800
The king might just get
His uncle Jaime back.

136
00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.440
-How?
-You love your children.

137
00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:14.800
It's your one redeeming quality.
That and your cheekbones.

138
00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:18.240
The Starks love
Their children as well.

139
00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:19.920
-and we have two of them.
-One.

140
00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.360
-One?
-Arya. little animal--
She disappeared.

141
00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:27.320
Disappeared?
What. in a puff of smoke?

142
00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:32.160
We had three Starks to trade.

143
00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:35.560
You chopped one's head off
And let another escape.

144
00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.640
Father would be furious.

145
00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.800
It must be odd for you...

146
00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:45.080
To be the disappointing child.

147
00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:52.360
( crow cawing )

148
00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.880
Leadranach:
My lord. may the old gods
Watch over your brother

149
00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:58.480
And all our northern sons.

150
00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:02.240
The walls of my holdfast
Will not stand the winter.

151
00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:06.240
The stones were last mortared
In the time of King Aerys.

152
00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.320
And I'm afraid the masons today

153
00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:11.960
Are not fit to carry
Their fathers' hammers.

154
00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:14.520
When I was a boy.
I remember seeing them

155
00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:18.720
Put up a new tower
At torrhen's square in a summer.

156
00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.680
Men worked back then.

157
00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.560
Today. my holdfast
Looks like it was built

158
00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.120
By drunk children.

159
00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:30.520
At night you can hear the wind
Howling through the gaps.

160
00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:32.080
Gods forbid it rains.

161
00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.840
Why. I might as well sleep
Beneath our waterfall.

162
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.800
Luwin:
Maintenance of a holdfast

163
00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.640
Generally falls to the lord
Of that holdfast.

164
00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.760
Generally. yes.
But I've sent all the young men off

165
00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:44.480
To fight Robb Stark's war.

166
00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.600
King Robb. And it's not his war.

167
00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.720
-He didn't choose it.
-Maybe not. my lord.

168
00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.840
But he called in his banners
And took the men.

169
00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.240
Bran:
Joffrey killed my father.

170
00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:57.200
Your liege lord.

171
00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:59.560
Do you remember your vows. Ser?

172
00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.200
Of course I remember!

173
00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:04.160
We can spare four masons
For a week. my lord.

174
00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:07.600
Will that be sufficient
To repair your walls?

175
00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.240
I-- I believe it will.

176
00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.320
We didn't want him here
All day. did we?

177
00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:21.520
I didn't like the way
He was talking about Robb.

178
00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.240
Nor did I.

179
00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.280
But listening to people
You'd rather not listen to

180
00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:32.000
Is one of your responsibilities
As lord of winterfell.

181
00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.800
( sighs )

182
00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:37.160
Luwin:
Lord Portan.

183
00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:40.040
My lord. may the old gods
Watch over your brother

184
00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.720
And all our northern sons.

185
00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.680
( heavy breathing )

186
00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.800
-( wings flapping )
-( bird squawking )

187
00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:33.200
Boil this for an hour
And drink the tea.

188
00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.480
Makes all your pain go away.

189
00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:39.280
-Bran: Don't have any pain.
-Lucky for you.

190
00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:42.320
That way.

191
00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.280
You've been having
Those dreams again.

192
00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:50.280
-Bran: I don't dream.
-Everyone dreams.

193
00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:53.280
I don't.

194
00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.840
Heard some of the men
Talking about the comet.

195
00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.360
They say it's an omen.

196
00:12:57.520 --> 00:13:00.600
They say it means Robb will win
A great victory in the south.

197
00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.200
Did they?

198
00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.640
Osha:
I heard some other fools
Say it's Lannister red.

199
00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:10.680
Means the Lannisters will rule
All seven kingdoms before long.

200
00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:14.000
Heard a stableboy say
It's the color of blood

201
00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.160
To mark the death of your father.

202
00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.280
The stars don't fall for men.

203
00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.680
The red comet means one thing. boy--

204
00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.640
Dragons.

205
00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.760
The dragons are all dead.

206
00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:35.040
They've been dead for centuries.

207
00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:08.800
( shrieks )

208
00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:12.480
Mmm.

209
00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:15.280
Mmm. Mmm.

210
00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:19.160
What did your brother say
about them. Khaleesi?

211
00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:20.880
He said they ate meat.

212
00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:24.520
He didn't tell you what kind of meat?

213
00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:27.720
My brother didn't know
Anything about dragons.

214
00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:30.680
He didn't know anything
About anything.

215
00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:37.440
Eh.

216
00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.520
( whinnies )

217
00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.440
( women murmuring )

218
00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.720
She was Drogo's first gift to me.

219
00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.480
I remember.

220
00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:12.040
I promised to protect them.

221
00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:14.120
Promised them
Their enemies would die screaming.

222
00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:16.640
How do I make starvation scream?

223
00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:19.560
A trick I never learned. I'm afraid.

224
00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.320
Does it ever end?

225
00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.160
This is further east
Than I've ever been.

226
00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.160
But. yes. Khaleesi.
Everything ends. even the red waste.

227
00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.720
And you're sure there's no other way?

228
00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:33.280
If we go south to the land
Of the Lazarheen.

229
00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:35.560
The lamb men will kill us
and take your dragons.

230
00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:37.360
If we go west to the Dothraki sea.

231
00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:39.480
The first Khalasar we meet

232
00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:41.000
Will kill us and take your dragons.

233
00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.440
No one will take my dragons.

234
00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:47.280
They are too weak to fight.

235
00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:49.360
As are your people.

236
00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:51.360
You must be their strength.

237
00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:54.320
As you are mine.

238
00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:00.200
( speaks Dothraki )

239
00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:08.480
( speaking Dothraki )

240
00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.760
( speaks Dothraki )

241
00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:42.200
Rakharo...

242
00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:52.160
You never have.

243
00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:59.400
This is bad time to start.

244
00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:14.920
( horse whinnies )

245
00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:39.680
( wind howling )

246
00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:44.160
( thunder rumbling )

247
00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:53.360
( bird caws )

248
00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:56.800
-Having a rough time of it?
-Nothing's killed me yet.

249
00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:59.120
-Grenn: your ass killed the sledge.
-You offered me a ride.

250
00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:02.240
I just wanted you to shut up
About your damn blisters.

251
00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:18.840
I was born in a place like this.

252
00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.000
Later. I fell on hard times.

253
00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:25.040
Samwell:
Are those girls?

254
00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.440
Dolorous edd:
Craster's daughters.

255
00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.440
I haven't seen a girl in six months.

256
00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:33.040
I'd keep on not seeing them
If I were you.

257
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.360
What. he don't like people messing
With his daughters?

258
00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:37.960
He don't like people
Messing with his wives.

259
00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:41.600
He marries his daughters.

260
00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:46.160
And they give him more daughters.
And on and on it goes.

261
00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:48.320
-That's foul.
-It's beyond foul.

262
00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:52.200
All the other wildlings
For a hundred leagues
Have disappeared.

263
00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.240
Craster's still here.

264
00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.640
He must be doing something right.

265
00:18:58.480 --> 00:18:59.920
What happens to the boys?

266
00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:03.440
-Hmm?
-He marries his daughters.

267
00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:06.160
What does he do with his sons?

268
00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:11.880
He said he planned to stop here
On his way to the Frostfangs.

269
00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:13.520
People make all sorts of plans.

270
00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:18.240
I haven't seen Benjen Stark
In three years. Haven't missed him.

271
00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:20.800
Always treated me like scum.

272
00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:24.800
Haven't had any good wine
For a long time.

273
00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:27.600
You southerners make good wine.
I'll give you that.

274
00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:29.560
We're not southerners.

275
00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:31.200
Who's this little girl?

276
00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:35.360
You're prettier
Than half my daughters.

277
00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.600
You got a nice wet twat
Between your legs?

278
00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:40.400
What's your name?

279
00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:42.600
-Jon Snow.
-Snow. eh?

280
00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:45.120
Listen to me. bastard.

281
00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:49.160
All you lot from south of the wall.
You're southerners.

282
00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:52.880
But now you're in the north.
The real north.

283
00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:54.400
The lad meant no harm.

284
00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.840
I catch that pretty little bastard
Talking to my daughters--

285
00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:02.880
No one will talk to your daughters.
You have my word.

286
00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:05.960
Now. sit down and shut your mouth.

287
00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:10.920
You bring any of that
Good wine with you?

288
00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:12.400
We did.

289
00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.960
We passed through
Six villages on the way here.

290
00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:17.720
All six were abandoned.

291
00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.800
Where have all the wildlings gone?

292
00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:23.440
I could tell you. but I'm thirsty.

293
00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:25.280
Mormont: there's a barrel of
Dornish wine on the sledge.

294
00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:27.880
-Bring it in here.
-Man: yes. commander.

295
00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.600
Craster: you want to know
Where they've all gone?

296
00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:34.600
North... To join up
With Mance Rayder...

297
00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:38.360
Your old friend.

298
00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:40.520
He's no friend of mine.

299
00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:42.240
He broke his vows.

300
00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:44.640
-betrayed his brothers.
-Oh. aye.

301
00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.720
But once he was
Just a poor black crow.

302
00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:50.560
And now he's king-beyond-the-wall.

303
00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.880
He's been calling
Himself that for years.

304
00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:56.400
What's he king of?
A frozen lake somewhere?

305
00:20:58.080 --> 00:20:59.920
That's a good looking axe.

306
00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:01.920
Fresh forged?

307
00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:06.280
Give it here.

308
00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:08.280
You'll have another one
Made at castle black.

309
00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:10.200
Here.

310
00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:13.720
Oh. that's some lovely steel.

311
00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:20.560
You want to know
What Mance Rayder is doing?

312
00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:22.600
Gathering an army.

313
00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:24.360
What I hear.
He's already got more men

314
00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:26.000
Than any of your southern kings.

315
00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:29.120
And where does he plan
Marching this army?

316
00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:33.000
When you're all the way north.
There's only one direction to go.

317
00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:38.960
These are bad times to be
Living alone in the wild.

318
00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:41.920
The cold winds are rising.

319
00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:45.280
Let them come.
My roots are sunk deep.

320
00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:48.840
Wife...

321
00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:53.120
Tell the lord crow
How content we are.

322
00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:54.920
This is our place.

323
00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.080
Our husband keeps us safe.

324
00:21:57.240 --> 00:22:00.160
Better to live free than die a slave.

325
00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:05.040
Craster:
Don't it make you jealous. old man.

326
00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:06.880
To see me with all these young wives

327
00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:10.240
And you with no one
To warm your bed?

328
00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:12.120
We chose different paths.

329
00:22:12.280 --> 00:22:16.240
Oh. aye. and you chose the path
With no one but boys on it.

330
00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:20.640
You'll be wanting to sleep
Beneath my roof. I suppose.

331
00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:23.040
And eat me out of pigs.

332
00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:24.920
A roof would be welcome.

333
00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:26.400
It's been hard riding.

334
00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:29.520
We've brought our own food
And good steel for you.

335
00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:35.520
Any man lays a hand
On one of my wives.

336
00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:38.320
He loses the hand.

337
00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:43.000
And I see this one staring too long.

338
00:22:43.160 --> 00:22:46.040
I might just gouge his eyes out.

339
00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:49.200
Your roof. your rules.

340
00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:01.720
( grunts )

341
00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:04.080
Who am I?!

342
00:23:04.240 --> 00:23:07.480
-Who am I?!
-Lord commander.

343
00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:10.440
-And who are you?
-Jon Snow.

344
00:23:10.600 --> 00:23:13.280
Who are you?

345
00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:15.080
Your steward.

346
00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:17.080
You want to lead one day?

347
00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:22.600
Then learn how to follow.

348
00:23:34.280 --> 00:23:37.160
( man panting )

349
00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:43.480
Melisandre: Lord of Light.
Come to us in our darkness.

350
00:23:43.640 --> 00:23:47.280
We offer you these false gods.

351
00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:49.760
Take them and cast
Your light upon us...

352
00:23:51.920 --> 00:23:55.600
For the night is dark
And full of terrors.

353
00:23:55.760 --> 00:23:58.880
Men: for the night is dark
And full of terrors.

354
00:24:01.200 --> 00:24:02.920
Melisandre:
After the long summer.

355
00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:05.720
Darkness will fall heavy
On the world.

356
00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:08.360
The stars will bleed.

357
00:24:08.520 --> 00:24:10.800
We need to stop her.

358
00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:15.040
Melisandre:
The cold breath of winter
Will freeze the seas...

359
00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:19.080
-Not now.
-...and the dead shall rise
In the north.

360
00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:23.800
All you men were named
In the light of the seven!

361
00:24:23.960 --> 00:24:26.760
Is this how you treat
The gods of your fathers?

362
00:24:26.920 --> 00:24:31.400
Are you so eager to spit
On your ancestors?

363
00:24:39.840 --> 00:24:41.800
You smell of fear--

364
00:24:41.960 --> 00:24:46.120
Fear and piss and old bones.

365
00:24:47.320 --> 00:24:48.880
Do you want to stop me?

366
00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:54.920
Stop me.

367
00:25:07.280 --> 00:25:08.760
In the ancient books. it's written

368
00:25:08.920 --> 00:25:12.560
That a warrior will draw
A burning sword from the fire.

369
00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:16.640
And that sword shall be
Lightbringer.

370
00:25:21.640 --> 00:25:24.920
Stannis Baratheon.

371
00:25:25.080 --> 00:25:27.320
Warrior of Light.

372
00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:29.160
your sword awaits you.

373
00:25:49.240 --> 00:25:51.280
( men cheering )

374
00:25:58.480 --> 00:26:01.640
Men:
Lord. cast your light upon us!

375
00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:06.160
Melisandre: for the night is dark
And full of terrors.

376
00:26:08.960 --> 00:26:12.040
For the night is dark
And full of terror.

377
00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:41.600
This woman will lead him
Into a war he cannot win.

378
00:26:41.760 --> 00:26:44.600
Stannis is our king.
We follow where he leads.

379
00:26:44.760 --> 00:26:47.400
-even if we don't like the path.
-King.

380
00:26:47.560 --> 00:26:49.120
Since that boar killed his brother.

381
00:26:49.280 --> 00:26:51.160
Every lord wants a coronation.

382
00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:53.320
I don't serve the others.
I serve Stannis.

383
00:26:53.480 --> 00:26:56.880
As do I. but loyal service

384
00:26:57.040 --> 00:26:59.480
Means telling hard truths.

385
00:26:59.640 --> 00:27:03.560
He's surrounded
By fools and fanatics.

386
00:27:03.720 --> 00:27:06.480
But he trusts you. Davos.

387
00:27:06.640 --> 00:27:09.320
If you tell him the truth...

388
00:27:10.960 --> 00:27:12.720
What's the truth?

389
00:27:24.760 --> 00:27:26.280
Matthos: "and I declare upon
The honor of my house

390
00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:30.040
-that my beloved brother Robert--"
-He wasn't my beloved brother.

391
00:27:30.200 --> 00:27:32.640
I didn't love him. He didn't love me.

392
00:27:32.800 --> 00:27:37.120
-A harmless courtesy. your Grace.
-A lie. Take it out.

393
00:27:38.560 --> 00:27:40.800
"...that my brother Robert
Left no trueborn heirs.

394
00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:42.400
The boy Joffrey. the boy Tommen.

395
00:27:42.560 --> 00:27:44.320
And the girl Myrcella
Being born of incest

396
00:27:44.480 --> 00:27:47.680
Between Cersei Lannister and
Her brother Jaime Lannister.

397
00:27:47.840 --> 00:27:50.240
-by right of birth--"
-Jaime Lannister. the Kingslayer.

398
00:27:50.400 --> 00:27:52.240
Call him what he is.

399
00:27:53.840 --> 00:27:56.200
Matthos: "...and her brother.
Jaime Lannister. the Kingslayer.

400
00:27:56.360 --> 00:27:59.240
By right of birth and blood.
I do this day lay claim--"

401
00:27:59.400 --> 00:28:02.160
Stannis:
Make it Ser Jaime Lannister.
The Kingslayer.

402
00:28:02.320 --> 00:28:04.320
Whatever else he is.
The man's still a knight.

403
00:28:04.480 --> 00:28:06.600
"Ser Jaime Lannister.
The Kingslayer.

404
00:28:06.760 --> 00:28:08.560
By right of birth and blood.

405
00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:12.000
I do this day lay claim
To the iron throne of Westeros.

406
00:28:12.160 --> 00:28:14.400
Let all true men
Declare their loyalty."

407
00:28:14.560 --> 00:28:16.480
When Eddard Stark learned
The truth. he told only me.

408
00:28:16.640 --> 00:28:18.720
I'll not make the same mistake.

409
00:28:18.880 --> 00:28:20.760
Send copies of that letter
To every corner of the realm.

410
00:28:20.920 --> 00:28:22.960
From the arbor to the wall.

411
00:28:23.120 --> 00:28:25.600
The time has come to choose.

412
00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:27.840
Let no man claim ignorance
As an excuse.

413
00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:30.280
Your Grace. the Lannisters
Are the true enemy.

414
00:28:30.440 --> 00:28:32.320
If. for the time being.
You could make peace
With your brother--

415
00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:34.480
I'll not make peace with Renly
While he calls himself king.

416
00:28:34.640 --> 00:28:36.280
Well. many have already
Declared for him--

417
00:28:36.440 --> 00:28:38.280
Mace Tyrell. Randyll Tarly.

418
00:28:38.440 --> 00:28:41.640
Stannis does not need to beg
This lord or that lord for support.

419
00:28:41.800 --> 00:28:43.200
The Lord of Light stands behind him.

420
00:28:43.360 --> 00:28:46.400
And how many ships
Has the Lord of Light
Got in his fleet?

421
00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:48.920
-He has no need for ships.
-I'm sure he doesn't.

422
00:28:49.080 --> 00:28:50.880
But we do if we're going to war.

423
00:28:51.040 --> 00:28:53.600
If not Renly. your Grace.
Join forces with Robb Stark.

424
00:28:53.760 --> 00:28:55.480
Who would steal
The northern half of my kingdom.

425
00:28:55.640 --> 00:28:57.320
I've always served thieves
According to their desserts.

426
00:28:57.480 --> 00:28:58.960
As you well know. Ser Davos.

427
00:28:59.120 --> 00:29:01.920
Joffrey. Renly. Robb Stark.
They're all thieves.

428
00:29:02.080 --> 00:29:05.160
They'll bend the knee
Or I'll destroy them.

429
00:29:05.320 --> 00:29:08.640
I owe you an apology. my king.

430
00:29:08.800 --> 00:29:10.640
My duty is to serve.

431
00:29:10.800 --> 00:29:14.680
You have chosen the new god
Over the old gods.

432
00:29:14.840 --> 00:29:18.080
May the Lord of Light
Watch over us all.

433
00:29:18.240 --> 00:29:20.720
Shall we drink together?

434
00:29:20.880 --> 00:29:22.400
Don't.

435
00:29:22.560 --> 00:29:27.040
A cup of wine to honor
The one true god.

436
00:30:07.440 --> 00:30:08.760
( thuds )

437
00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:11.040
( men murmuring )

438
00:30:11.200 --> 00:30:14.680
The night is dark and full
Of terrors. old man.

439
00:30:14.840 --> 00:30:17.760
But the fire burns them all away.

440
00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:24.760
( chatter )

441
00:30:38.600 --> 00:30:40.400
Man:
Your Grace.

442
00:30:51.040 --> 00:30:53.520
King in the north.

443
00:30:55.440 --> 00:30:56.760
I keep expecting you to leave me

444
00:30:56.920 --> 00:30:58.720
In one castle or another
For safekeeping.

445
00:30:58.880 --> 00:31:03.280
But you drag me along
From camp to camp.

446
00:31:03.440 --> 00:31:05.400
Have you grown fond of me. Stark?

447
00:31:05.560 --> 00:31:07.200
Is that it?

448
00:31:07.360 --> 00:31:09.000
I've never seen you with a girl.

449
00:31:10.360 --> 00:31:12.560
If I left you with
One of my bannermen.

450
00:31:12.720 --> 00:31:15.560
Your father would know
Within a fortnight

451
00:31:15.720 --> 00:31:19.040
And my bannerman would receive
A raven with a message:

452
00:31:19.200 --> 00:31:22.360
"release my son and you'll be rich
Beyond your dreams.

453
00:31:22.520 --> 00:31:25.960
Refuse and your house
Will be destroyed. root and stem."

454
00:31:26.120 --> 00:31:27.800
You don't trust the loyalty

455
00:31:27.960 --> 00:31:30.120
Of the men following
You into battle?

456
00:31:30.280 --> 00:31:33.720
Oh. I trust them with my life.

457
00:31:33.880 --> 00:31:35.440
Just not with yours.

458
00:31:35.600 --> 00:31:37.520
Smart boy.

459
00:31:37.680 --> 00:31:39.160
What's wrong?

460
00:31:39.320 --> 00:31:40.880
Don't like being called "boy"?

461
00:31:41.800 --> 00:31:43.600
Insulted?

462
00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:50.440
( direwolf snarling )

463
00:31:50.600 --> 00:31:52.840
Robb:
You insult yourself. Kingslayer.

464
00:31:55.080 --> 00:31:58.080
-You've been defeated by a boy.
-( heavy breathing )

465
00:31:58.240 --> 00:32:00.360
You're held captive by a boy.

466
00:32:03.120 --> 00:32:05.440
Perhaps you'll be killed by a boy.

467
00:32:11.600 --> 00:32:13.040
Stannis Baratheon sent ravens

468
00:32:13.200 --> 00:32:16.600
To all the high lords of Westeros.

469
00:32:16.760 --> 00:32:20.080
King Joffrey Baratheon
Is neither a true king

470
00:32:20.240 --> 00:32:23.040
Nor a true Baratheon.

471
00:32:23.200 --> 00:32:24.680
He's your bastard son.

472
00:32:24.840 --> 00:32:27.000
If that's true.
Stannis is the rightful king.

473
00:32:27.160 --> 00:32:29.000
How convenient for him.

474
00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:33.040
My father learned the truth.

475
00:32:33.200 --> 00:32:34.640
That's why you had him executed.

476
00:32:34.800 --> 00:32:37.120
I was your prisoner
When Ned Stark lost his head.

477
00:32:37.280 --> 00:32:39.000
Your son killed him

478
00:32:39.160 --> 00:32:40.680
So the world wouldn't
Learn who fathered him.

479
00:32:40.840 --> 00:32:44.480
And you-- you pushed
My brother from a window

480
00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:46.240
Because he saw you with the queen.

481
00:32:47.800 --> 00:32:49.520
( snarling )

482
00:32:51.280 --> 00:32:54.200
You have proof?

483
00:32:54.360 --> 00:32:56.640
Or do you want to trade gossip
Like a couple of fishwives?

484
00:32:56.800 --> 00:32:58.560
I'm sending one of your cousins
Down to King’s Landing

485
00:32:58.720 --> 00:33:00.320
With my peace terms.

486
00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:03.680
You think my father's going
To negotiate with you?

487
00:33:03.840 --> 00:33:05.720
You don't know him very well.

488
00:33:05.880 --> 00:33:10.240
No. but he's starting to know me.

489
00:33:10.400 --> 00:33:13.480
Three victories
Don't make you a conqueror.

490
00:33:14.960 --> 00:33:17.320
It's better than three defeats.

491
00:33:22.400 --> 00:33:25.640
( snarling )

492
00:33:44.640 --> 00:33:47.040
Shae:
This city stinks...

493
00:33:47.200 --> 00:33:49.360
( sniffs )

494
00:33:49.520 --> 00:33:50.960
Like dead bodies.

495
00:33:51.120 --> 00:33:52.960
Tyrion:
A bit corpsey. yes.

496
00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:55.520
And shit.

497
00:33:55.680 --> 00:33:57.080
I thought you wanted to come here.

498
00:34:00.680 --> 00:34:02.960
I love it.

499
00:34:03.120 --> 00:34:06.440
You love the smell
Of dead bodies and shit?

500
00:34:06.600 --> 00:34:09.400
And cum and garlic and rum.

501
00:34:09.560 --> 00:34:12.280
You can smell cum
From the balcony?

502
00:34:12.440 --> 00:34:15.760
I love the stink. I love the noise.

503
00:34:15.920 --> 00:34:18.480
Cities make me want to fuck.

504
00:34:18.640 --> 00:34:20.600
And so did the country.

505
00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:23.720
( sighs )

506
00:34:23.880 --> 00:34:25.280
This is where I belong.

507
00:34:25.440 --> 00:34:28.160
Yes. well. you need to be careful.

508
00:34:28.320 --> 00:34:31.080
-No one can know you're here.
-No one will know.

509
00:34:31.240 --> 00:34:32.760
You can't trust anyone
In King’s Landing.

510
00:34:32.920 --> 00:34:35.680
They're all liars--
Good liars. bad liars.

511
00:34:35.840 --> 00:34:38.080
One or two great liars.

512
00:34:38.240 --> 00:34:39.960
What about you?

513
00:34:40.120 --> 00:34:42.760
Me? I'm not from here.
I'm a slave to the truth.

514
00:34:43.320 --> 00:34:45.320
( laughs )
Truth?

515
00:34:45.480 --> 00:34:50.080
( laughs ) you are the biggest
Little liar I have ever met.

516
00:34:50.240 --> 00:34:52.040
Why do you think I am so little?

517
00:34:52.200 --> 00:34:56.280
I'm being crushed
Beneath the weight of all that truth.

518
00:34:58.600 --> 00:35:00.520
Oh!

519
00:35:00.680 --> 00:35:03.400
Ned Stark actually slept on this.

520
00:35:03.560 --> 00:35:06.600
As if the poor man
Didn't suffer enough.

521
00:35:08.720 --> 00:35:11.880
One of the many changes
We'll have to make around here.

522
00:35:22.840 --> 00:35:26.000
-Lord Baelish.
-Your Grace.

523
00:35:26.160 --> 00:35:28.480
I wonder if I might
Ask you for a favor.

524
00:35:28.640 --> 00:35:31.880
-Of course. your Grace.
-Ned Stark's youngest daughter Arya--

525
00:35:32.040 --> 00:35:34.400
We can't seem to locate her.

526
00:35:34.560 --> 00:35:36.240
If she's escaped the capital.

527
00:35:36.400 --> 00:35:38.240
Winterfell seems
The logical destination.

528
00:35:38.400 --> 00:35:41.000
And yet my friends in the north
Report no sign of her.

529
00:35:41.160 --> 00:35:42.760
Curious.

530
00:35:42.920 --> 00:35:44.840
If we choose to negotiate
With the Starks.

531
00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:46.840
The girl has some value.
Whoever finds her--

532
00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:48.760
Well. you know what they say about
Lannisters and debts.

533
00:35:48.920 --> 00:35:52.200
Well. you could ask
Varys where she is.

534
00:35:52.360 --> 00:35:54.760
He'll have an answer for you.
Whether you believe it...

535
00:35:54.920 --> 00:35:58.840
Myself. I have always had
A hard time trusting eunuchs.

536
00:35:59.000 --> 00:36:01.320
-Who knows what they want?
-( chuckles )

537
00:36:01.480 --> 00:36:04.440
A mockingbird.

538
00:36:04.600 --> 00:36:08.040
-You created your
Own sigil. didn't you?
-Yes.

539
00:36:08.200 --> 00:36:10.000
Appropriate... For a self-made man

540
00:36:10.160 --> 00:36:11.680
With so many songs to sing.

541
00:36:11.840 --> 00:36:13.480
I'm glad you like it.

542
00:36:13.640 --> 00:36:16.920
Some people are fortunate enough
To be born into the right family.

543
00:36:17.080 --> 00:36:19.160
Others have to find their own way.

544
00:36:20.720 --> 00:36:22.640
I heard a song once

545
00:36:22.800 --> 00:36:25.240
About a boy of modest means

546
00:36:25.400 --> 00:36:27.640
Who found his way into the home
Of a very prominent family.

547
00:36:29.160 --> 00:36:34.200
He loved the eldest daughter.
Sadly. she had eyes for another.

548
00:36:34.360 --> 00:36:36.160
When boys and girls
Live in the same home.

549
00:36:36.320 --> 00:36:38.640
Awkward situations can arise.

550
00:36:38.800 --> 00:36:41.200
Sometimes. I've heard.
Even brothers and sisters

551
00:36:41.360 --> 00:36:43.600
Develop certain affections.

552
00:36:43.760 --> 00:36:46.000
And when these affections
Become common knowledge.

553
00:36:46.160 --> 00:36:49.720
Well. that is an awkward
Situation indeed.

554
00:36:49.880 --> 00:36:51.880
Especially in a prominent family.

555
00:36:52.040 --> 00:36:55.240
But prominent families
Often forget a simple truth.

556
00:36:55.400 --> 00:36:57.480
I've found.

557
00:36:57.640 --> 00:36:59.480
And which truth is that?

558
00:36:59.640 --> 00:37:02.920
Knowledge is power.

559
00:37:05.280 --> 00:37:07.320
Seize him.

560
00:37:09.600 --> 00:37:11.520
Cut his throat.

561
00:37:11.680 --> 00:37:14.840
Stop. Wait.

562
00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:16.760
I've changed my mind. Let him go.

563
00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:21.200
Step back three paces.

564
00:37:22.920 --> 00:37:25.200
Turn around.

565
00:37:25.360 --> 00:37:27.120
Close your eyes.

566
00:37:30.680 --> 00:37:33.200
Power is power.

567
00:37:34.720 --> 00:37:38.080
Do see if you can take some time
Away from your coins and your whores

568
00:37:38.240 --> 00:37:40.080
To locate the Stark girl for me.

569
00:37:40.240 --> 00:37:43.280
I would very much appreciate it.

570
00:37:53.280 --> 00:37:55.560
Robb:
You're Ser Alton Lannister?

571
00:37:55.720 --> 00:37:57.520
I am. your Grace.

572
00:37:57.680 --> 00:38:00.960
I offer your cousins peace
If they meet my terms.

573
00:38:01.120 --> 00:38:05.720
First. your family
Must release my sisters.

574
00:38:05.880 --> 00:38:08.440
Second. my father's bones
Must be returned to us

575
00:38:08.600 --> 00:38:10.520
So he may rest beside
His brother and sister

576
00:38:10.680 --> 00:38:12.840
In the crypts beneath Winterfell.

577
00:38:13.000 --> 00:38:15.080
And the remains of all those
Who died in his service

578
00:38:15.240 --> 00:38:17.440
Must also be returned.

579
00:38:17.600 --> 00:38:19.920
Their families can honor
Them with proper funerals.

580
00:38:20.080 --> 00:38:22.720
-An honorable request. your Grace.
-Third...

581
00:38:24.520 --> 00:38:26.640
Joffrey and the queen regent
Must renounce all claim

582
00:38:26.800 --> 00:38:29.320
To dominion of the north.

583
00:38:29.480 --> 00:38:31.280
From this time till the end of time.

584
00:38:31.440 --> 00:38:33.760
We are a free
And independent kingdom.

585
00:38:33.920 --> 00:38:35.760
The king in the north.

586
00:38:35.920 --> 00:38:38.160
All:
King in the north.

587
00:38:38.320 --> 00:38:39.680
Neither Joffrey nor any of his men

588
00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:41.800
Shall set foot in our lands again.

589
00:38:41.960 --> 00:38:43.800
If he disregards this command.

590
00:38:43.960 --> 00:38:47.160
He shall suffer
The same fate as my father.

591
00:38:47.320 --> 00:38:51.320
Only I don't need a servant
To do my beheading for me.

592
00:38:51.480 --> 00:38:54.640
These are-- your Grace. these are--

593
00:38:54.800 --> 00:38:57.120
These are my terms.

594
00:38:57.280 --> 00:39:00.160
If the queen regent
And her son meet them.
I'll give them peace.

595
00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:03.120
If not...

596
00:39:03.280 --> 00:39:05.520
I will litter the south
With Lannister dead.

597
00:39:05.680 --> 00:39:08.200
King Joffrey
Is a Baratheon. your Grace.

598
00:39:08.360 --> 00:39:09.880
Oh. is he?

599
00:39:11.200 --> 00:39:14.080
You'll ride at daybreak. Ser Alton.

600
00:39:14.240 --> 00:39:16.800
That will be all for tonight.

601
00:39:31.360 --> 00:39:33.280
A word. your Grace?

602
00:39:34.840 --> 00:39:37.360
You don't have to
Call me "your Grace"
When no one's around.

603
00:39:37.520 --> 00:39:40.320
It's not so bad
Once you get used to it.

604
00:39:40.480 --> 00:39:42.920
I'm glad someone's gotten used to it.

605
00:39:43.080 --> 00:39:45.000
The Lannisters are going to reject
Your terms. you know?

606
00:39:45.160 --> 00:39:46.840
Of course they are.

607
00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:49.320
We can fight them
In the fields as long as you like.

608
00:39:49.480 --> 00:39:52.680
But we won't beat them
Until you take King’s Landing.

609
00:39:54.320 --> 00:39:57.160
And we can't take
King’s Landing without ships.

610
00:39:57.320 --> 00:39:59.640
My father has ships
And men who know how to sail them.

611
00:39:59.800 --> 00:40:01.440
Men who fought my father.

612
00:40:01.600 --> 00:40:03.640
Men who fought King Robert
To free themselves

613
00:40:03.800 --> 00:40:07.560
From the yoke of the south.
Just like you're doing now.

614
00:40:08.800 --> 00:40:11.480
I'm his only living son.

615
00:40:11.640 --> 00:40:14.800
He'll listen to me. I know he will.

616
00:40:17.240 --> 00:40:20.200
I'm not a Stark. I know that.

617
00:40:20.360 --> 00:40:22.920
But your father raised me
To be an honorable man.

618
00:40:24.840 --> 00:40:27.600
We can avenge him together.

619
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:31.000
You don't want Balon Greyjoy
For an ally.

620
00:40:31.160 --> 00:40:33.280
I need his ships.
They say he has 200.

621
00:40:33.440 --> 00:40:37.120
They say a million rats
Live in the sewers of King’s Landing.

622
00:40:37.280 --> 00:40:38.600
Shall we rally them to fight for us?

623
00:40:38.760 --> 00:40:40.480
I understand you don't
Trust Lord Greyjoy.

624
00:40:40.640 --> 00:40:45.000
I don't trust Lord Greyjoy
Because he is not trustworthy.

625
00:40:45.160 --> 00:40:47.480
Your father had to go to war
To end his rebellion.

626
00:40:47.640 --> 00:40:51.200
Yes. And now I'm the one
Rebelling against the throne.

627
00:40:51.360 --> 00:40:53.400
Before me. it was father.

628
00:40:53.560 --> 00:40:55.440
You married one rebel
And mothered another.

629
00:40:55.600 --> 00:40:58.000
I mothered more than just rebels.

630
00:40:58.160 --> 00:41:00.400
A fact you seem to have forgotten.

631
00:41:00.560 --> 00:41:02.480
If I trade the Kingslayer
For two girls.

632
00:41:02.640 --> 00:41:04.360
My bannermen
Will string me up by my feet.

633
00:41:04.520 --> 00:41:07.520
You want to leave Sansa
In the queen's hands?

634
00:41:07.680 --> 00:41:09.560
And Arya--

635
00:41:09.720 --> 00:41:12.600
I haven't heard a word about Arya.

636
00:41:12.760 --> 00:41:14.120
What are we fighting for
If not for them?

637
00:41:14.280 --> 00:41:17.680
It's more complicated than that!
You know it is.

638
00:41:31.720 --> 00:41:35.040
It's time for me to go home.

639
00:41:35.200 --> 00:41:38.080
I haven't seen Bran
Or Rickon in months.

640
00:41:39.040 --> 00:41:42.120
You can't go to Winterfell.

641
00:41:42.280 --> 00:41:43.600
I beg your pardon?

642
00:41:43.760 --> 00:41:46.480
I'll send Rodrik
To watch over the boys

643
00:41:46.640 --> 00:41:51.160
Because tomorrow
You'll ride south
To the Stormlands.

644
00:41:51.320 --> 00:41:52.800
Why in the name of all the gods--

645
00:41:52.960 --> 00:41:56.640
Because I need you to negotiate
With Renly Baratheon.

646
00:41:56.800 --> 00:41:58.760
He's rallied an army of 100.000.

647
00:41:58.920 --> 00:42:00.360
You know him. You know his family.

648
00:42:00.520 --> 00:42:02.600
I haven't seen Renly Baratheon
Since he was a boy.

649
00:42:02.760 --> 00:42:04.080
You have a hundred other lords--

650
00:42:04.240 --> 00:42:08.040
Which of these lords
Do I trust more than you?

651
00:42:08.200 --> 00:42:10.600
If Renly sides with us.

652
00:42:10.760 --> 00:42:13.000
We'll outnumber them two to one.

653
00:42:13.160 --> 00:42:15.920
When they feel
The jaws beginning to shut.
They'll sue for peace.

654
00:42:16.080 --> 00:42:18.560
We'll get the girls back.

655
00:42:18.720 --> 00:42:21.800
Then we'll all go home... For good.

656
00:42:28.760 --> 00:42:31.720
( sighs )
I will ride at first light.

657
00:42:40.080 --> 00:42:43.440
We will all be together
Again soon. I promise.

658
00:42:48.360 --> 00:42:50.600
You've done so well.

659
00:42:52.040 --> 00:42:55.440
Your father would be... Proud.

660
00:43:03.280 --> 00:43:05.760
-Give lord Renly my regards.
-King Renly.

661
00:43:07.200 --> 00:43:09.680
There's a king in every corner now.

662
00:43:11.480 --> 00:43:14.360
( hammering )

663
00:43:22.480 --> 00:43:24.520
What is all this?

664
00:43:24.680 --> 00:43:26.880
Returning this room
To its proper appearance.

665
00:43:27.040 --> 00:43:29.840
Say what you will
About the Targaryens--
They were conquerors.

666
00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.320
That is a seat for a conqueror.

667
00:43:32.480 --> 00:43:36.040
It needs a room to match it.
Not vines and flowers.

668
00:43:36.200 --> 00:43:38.200
We can't find Arya Stark.

669
00:43:38.360 --> 00:43:40.200
With luck. she's dead
In a ditch somewhere.

670
00:43:40.360 --> 00:43:42.240
Perhaps. But if not. we need her.

671
00:43:42.400 --> 00:43:44.520
They'll never give Jaime back to us
For Sansa alone.

672
00:43:44.680 --> 00:43:46.960
I think they might. They're weak.

673
00:43:47.120 --> 00:43:49.680
They put too much value
On their women.

674
00:43:49.840 --> 00:43:52.440
We need to set our armies
To the task of finding her.

675
00:43:52.600 --> 00:43:54.400
Send out as many men as we can.

676
00:43:54.560 --> 00:43:56.080
I'm sure if you asked grandfather--

677
00:43:56.240 --> 00:44:00.160
The king does not ask; he commands.

678
00:44:00.320 --> 00:44:02.680
And my grandfather's
Stupidity in the field of battle

679
00:44:02.840 --> 00:44:05.600
Is the reason Robb Stark
Has uncle Jaime in the first place.

680
00:44:05.760 --> 00:44:08.200
His life is in danger.

681
00:44:08.360 --> 00:44:09.840
We're at war.

682
00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:12.680
All our lives are in danger.

683
00:44:15.760 --> 00:44:19.280
I heard a disgusting lie
About uncle Jaime.

684
00:44:19.440 --> 00:44:21.680
And you.

685
00:44:21.840 --> 00:44:25.160
Our enemies will say anything
To weaken your claim to the throne.

686
00:44:25.320 --> 00:44:27.120
It's not a claim. The throne is mine.

687
00:44:28.880 --> 00:44:30.800
Of course it is.

688
00:44:32.440 --> 00:44:36.240
-No one believes this foul gossip.
-Someone believes it.

689
00:44:37.720 --> 00:44:40.200
Father had other children?

690
00:44:40.360 --> 00:44:42.440
Besides me and Tommen and Myrcella?

691
00:44:44.800 --> 00:44:46.200
What are you asking?

692
00:44:46.360 --> 00:44:50.000
I'm asking if he fucked other women
When he grew tired of you.

693
00:44:50.160 --> 00:44:51.760
How many bastards
Does he have running--

694
00:44:51.920 --> 00:44:54.520
( silence )

695
00:44:59.880 --> 00:45:02.200
( work resumes )

696
00:45:07.040 --> 00:45:10.880
What you just did
Is punishable by death.

697
00:45:14.400 --> 00:45:16.840
You will never do it again.

698
00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:18.600
Never.

699
00:45:24.600 --> 00:45:26.520
That will be all. mother.

700
00:45:30.760 --> 00:45:32.840
( loud moaning )

701
00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:34.840
No. no. no. no.

702
00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:37.640
Do you have any idea
How ridiculous you sound?

703
00:45:37.800 --> 00:45:42.000
Ease into it.
Slowly. with passion.

704
00:45:42.160 --> 00:45:45.640
( moaning )
Oh. yeah.

705
00:45:45.800 --> 00:45:49.360
( sighs )
Go wash yourselves.
Put some clothes on.

706
00:45:49.520 --> 00:45:51.840
Both of you are working tonight.

707
00:45:55.640 --> 00:45:57.440
We do things differently here. daisy.

708
00:45:57.600 --> 00:46:01.240
This isn't some
Five-copper bawdy house
In hayseed hall.

709
00:46:01.400 --> 00:46:03.720
-Haystack hall.
-Wherever you're from.

710
00:46:03.880 --> 00:46:05.520
Our establishment doesn't cater

711
00:46:05.680 --> 00:46:08.120
To ploughmen and goat herders.

712
00:46:08.280 --> 00:46:10.280
Lord Olsen.

713
00:46:10.440 --> 00:46:11.920
Taste is everything here.

714
00:46:12.080 --> 00:46:13.720
Littlefinger's a fancy man.

715
00:46:13.880 --> 00:46:16.840
Don't call him Littlefinger.
He doesn't like it.

716
00:46:17.000 --> 00:46:19.160
Lord Baelish.

717
00:46:24.360 --> 00:46:26.680
She pretends she doesn't
Speak the common tongue

718
00:46:26.840 --> 00:46:29.200
So that people
Will think she's exotic.

719
00:46:29.360 --> 00:46:32.800
She grew up just down the road
In flea bottom.

720
00:46:32.960 --> 00:46:34.440
She's beautiful.

721
00:46:34.600 --> 00:46:37.680
She's a dumb slut. really.
But a lid for every pot.

722
00:46:37.840 --> 00:46:39.200
( armor rattling )

723
00:46:42.600 --> 00:46:44.760
Lord commander.

724
00:46:44.920 --> 00:46:47.600
Good to see you... Again.

725
00:46:52.640 --> 00:46:54.200
( snaps fingers )

726
00:47:00.480 --> 00:47:01.840
-( door breaks )
-( woman screams )

727
00:47:02.000 --> 00:47:05.800
You do realize this establishment
Is owned by lord Petyr Baelish.

728
00:47:05.960 --> 00:47:08.000
The king's master of coin...

729
00:47:08.160 --> 00:47:09.800
Coin which goes in many pockets.

730
00:47:09.960 --> 00:47:12.400
-Orders.
-Whose orders?

731
00:47:12.560 --> 00:47:15.280
Someone who doesn't care
What Littlefinger thinks.

732
00:47:15.440 --> 00:47:17.200
( patrons whispering )

733
00:47:19.320 --> 00:47:21.760
( whimpering. crying )

734
00:47:21.920 --> 00:47:24.840
( baby crying )

735
00:47:32.360 --> 00:47:35.640
No. you can't. No! Please!

736
00:47:35.800 --> 00:47:38.280
No! Not my barra!

737
00:47:38.440 --> 00:47:41.680
-Please. Please.
-Enough. Get it done.

738
00:47:41.840 --> 00:47:43.560
-Kill the bastard.
-Mhaegen: no. no!

739
00:47:43.720 --> 00:47:45.920
-Please.
-Give it here.

740
00:47:46.080 --> 00:47:48.520
No. please.

741
00:47:48.680 --> 00:47:50.400
-( squelches )
-( screaming )

742
00:47:58.160 --> 00:48:00.160
Man:
Spread out. Search every house.

743
00:48:00.320 --> 00:48:02.480
Every room. Look in every room.

744
00:48:04.080 --> 00:48:06.440
( grunting )

745
00:48:08.280 --> 00:48:11.080
( women screaming )

746
00:48:15.600 --> 00:48:18.400
( people shouting )

747
00:48:26.240 --> 00:48:28.600
Gendry! His name is Gendry.

748
00:48:28.760 --> 00:48:30.320
Where is the bastard?

749
00:48:30.480 --> 00:48:34.320
-The night's watch! Please. stop!
-Where?

750
00:48:34.480 --> 00:48:37.240
They took him up the kingsroad.
Heading north.

751
00:48:37.400 --> 00:48:40.720
-How will we know him?
-He's got a bull's head helmet.

752
00:48:40.880 --> 00:48:43.560
-He made it himself.
-Find him.

753
00:49:16.480 --> 00:49:18.880
( theme music playing )
